'''Orondia Refueling Station''' was a filling station located on the [[planet]] [[Orondia]]. Owned by a [[Unidentified Bith filling station owner|Bith]], the station served as a fuel stop for [[starship]]s during the [[Clone Wars]].

==Description==
The filling station was a large refueling structure on the Orondia plains, featuring several starship berths surrounding the central station.<ref name="Friends and Enemies" />

==History==
{{Quote|So you only gave them enough fuel to reach the nearest filling station on Orondia, which is owned by your brother? Well, that's a nice little money-making scam.|Anakin Skywalker to a Bith merchant|<ref name="Friends and Enemies" />}}
Posing as the [[mercenary]] Rako Hardeen, [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] purchased a ship from a [[Bith]] [[Unidentified Bith starship dealer/Canon|merchant]] in [[Bilbousa]] on [[Nal Hutta]], in order to assist [[Cad Bane]] in escorting [[Moralo Eval]]. The merchant ensured the ship had only enough fuel to reach the filling station on Orondia owned by [[Unidentified Bith filling station owner|his brother]]. Upon arrival in their [[Personal Luxury Yacht 3000|Luxury 3000 space yacht]], Eval paid the station owner and made for departure, but the crew was spotted by [[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Ahsoka Tano]], who gave chase across the plains.<ref name="Friends and Enemies" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Orondia filling station first appeared in "[[Friends and Enemies]]," a [[2012]] episode of the television series [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars|''The Clone Wars'']]. The station's design was derived from [[Dave Filoni]]'s concept of a gray and bleak location he imagined [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] might have visited after the events of [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars:'' Episode IV ''A New Hope'']]. The design was also inspired by the truck stop/gas station from the 1995 animated film [[Wikipedia:Toy Story|''Toy Story'']].<ref name="FaE Trivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/friends-and-enemies-trivia-gallery|text="Friends and Enemies" Trivia Gallery}} (slide 10 of 11)</ref>

